When new reports are added to an already-linked visit, use the **Link context notify** endpoint to update ABDM with the new document types.

**Call:** `POST /api/hiecm/hip/v3/link/context/notify`

**Send:**
```json
{
  "notification": {
    "patient": {
      "id": "<ABHA_ADDRESS>"
    },
    "careContext": {
      "patientReference": "<ABHA_ADDRESS>",
      "careContextReference": "<care_context_id>"
    },
    "hiTypes": [
      "DiagnosticReport",
      "OPConsultation",
      ...
    ],
    "hip": {
      "id": "<your_hip_id>"
    },
    "date": "2024-05-09T10:34:00.387Z"
  }
}
```

**Key points:**
- `hiTypes`: Include all document types now in this care context, including the newly added ones. Pick from: DiagnosticReport, DischargeSummary, HealthDocumentRecord, ImmunizationRecord, OPConsultation, Prescription, WellnessRecord, Invoice
- `careContextReference`: Same as the original link
- `date`: UTC timestamp of the notification
- **Headers:** REQUEST-ID, TIMESTAMP, X-CM-ID, X-HIP-ID (same as your other calls)

The outcome arrives at `/api/v3/links/context/on-notify` on your bridge.

See the [Link context notify endpoint](https://abdm-docs.eka.care/docs/hiecm/v3/api/m2/endpoints/m2-post-hip-v3-link-context-notify) in the ABDM developer portal.

